## The idea

Fix one point and look at the direction to every other point. Points on the same line through the fixed point have the **same direction**. Store each direction as an exact fraction dy/dx reduced by their greatest common divisor, with one sign convention, and count how many points share it. Exact integers avoid the classic bug where nearly equal slopes compare equal as doubles. Duplicate points lie on every line, so they are added to the best count.

## Step by step

1. For each point i: create an empty dictionary direction → count, and duplicates = 0.
2. For each later point j: dy = yj − yi, dx = xj − xi (as long, to avoid overflow). If both are 0, it is a duplicate.
3. Otherwise divide dy and dx by gcd(|dy|, |dx|), and make dx positive (or dy positive when dx = 0), so (1,2) and (−1,−2) look the same. Count this direction.
4. Points on the best line through i = biggest count + duplicates + 1 (point i itself). Keep the overall maximum.

## Worked example

**Input:** (1,1), (2,2), (3,3), (1,0)

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| from (1,1) | (2,2): dy 1, dx 1 → (1,1) count 1; (3,3): dy 2, dx 2 → gcd 2 → (1,1) count 2; (1,0): dy −1, dx 0 → (1,0) vertical, count 1 |
| best through (1,1) | 2 + 0 duplicates + 1 = 3 |
| other points | cannot beat 3 |

**Result:** 3

## Cost

O(n²) time (every pair once, with a gcd of O(log value)). O(n) memory for the dictionary.

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
public static class MaxPoints {

    public static int OnALine(int[][] points) {
        if (points == null) return 0;
        int n = points.Length;
        if (n <= 2) return n;

        int best = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            Dictionary<string, int> directions = new Dictionary<string, int>();
            int duplicates = 0;
            int bestHere = 0;

            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                long dy = (long)points[j][1] - points[i][1];   // long: extreme coordinates overflow int
                long dx = (long)points[j][0] - points[i][0];
                if (dy == 0 && dx == 0) {
                    duplicates++;                                // same point: on every line through i
                    continue;
                }
                long g = Gcd(Math.Abs(dy), Math.Abs(dx));
                dy /= g;
                dx /= g;
                // one sign convention, so (1,2) and (-1,-2) are the same direction
                if (dx < 0 || (dx == 0 && dy < 0)) {
                    dy = -dy;
                    dx = -dx;
                }
                string key = dy + "/" + dx;
                int count = 1;
                if (directions.ContainsKey(key)) count = directions[key] + 1;
                directions[key] = count;
                if (count > bestHere) bestHere = count;
            }

            int onBestLine = bestHere + duplicates + 1;          // +1 for point i itself
            if (onBestLine > best) best = onBestLine;
        }
        return best;
    }

    private static long Gcd(long a, long b) {
        while (b != 0) {
            long t = a % b;
            a = b;
            b = t;
        }
        return a;
    }
}
```

